[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Pretty Carpet]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:09.89]What is the writer's carpet made of? | 作者的“地毯”是用什么做的？
[00:14.42]We have just moved into a new house and I have been working hard all morning. | 我们刚刚搬进一所新房子，我辛辛苦苦地干了整整一个上午。
[00:22.27]I have been trying to get my new room in order. | 我一直试图把我的新房间收拾整齐。
[00:27.17]This has not been easy because I own over a thousand books. | 这活儿可不容易，因为我有1,000多本书。
[00:34.01]To make matters worse, | 更糟糕的是，
[00:36.02]the room is rather small, | 房间还特别小，
[00:38.71]so I have temporarily put my books on the floor. | 所以我暂时把书堆在了地板上。
[00:44.30]At the moment, they cover every inch of floor space | 这会儿，书占据了每一寸地板，
[00:48.83]and I actually have to walk on them to get in or out of the room. | 我进出房间实际上得踩着书走。
[00:55.80]A short while ago, my sister helped me to carry one of my old bookcases up the stairs. | 刚才，我妹妹帮我把一个旧书柜抬上了楼。
[01:04.52]She went into my room and got a big surprise when she saw all those books on the floor. | 她走进我的房间，看到地板上堆满了书，大吃一惊。
[01:13.35]'This is the prettiest carpet I have ever seen,' she said. | “这是我见过的最漂亮的地毯，”她说。
[01:19.77]She gazed at it for some time then added, | 她盯着“地毯”看了一会儿又说：
[01:24.03]'You don't need bookcases at all. | “你根本用不着书柜了。
[01:27.25]You can sit here in your spare time and read the carpet!' | 空闲时你可以坐在这儿读地毯！”
